+# Decision: the lab is the central Scope, and the processes it keeps
+
+Decided by Justin on 4 October 2026, in the afternoon, in an interview. At the time these were written only into
+`STATE.md`, which is overwritten at each verified event. Copied here on 7 October 2026 by the entropy-guard assessment,
+in the words `STATE.md` held on 4 October at 17:31. Copying them is not deciding them again; nothing below is new.
+
+## Decided on 4 October
+
+- **The lab is the central Scope** for project management, core issue tracking, code quality and security. Astra is to
+  say what else it should cover. *(Open: what else it covers.)*
+- **Where issues live:** a Scope's issues stay in its own repository, on one central map; a `core` label marks a Scope
+  issue that needs ORC's core changed. Later, Scopes may track their own business logic elsewhere.
+- **The processes kept, all of them:**
+  - map and label check;
+  - tests on every PR (#144);
+  - the security-review and package-API checks;
+  - daily diary;
+  - weekly adversarial review;
+  - entropy guard at session end;
+  - FRICTION into rules, monthly (#60);
+  - branch and worktree cleanup (#70);
+  - `/tmp` cleanup (#182).
+- **ORC scheduling (#166) is built first,** and the scheduled ones run through it.
+- **Astra runs entropy-guard's assessment on ORC and the lab together.** Justin is shaping the brief before it runs.
+- **MS is paused:** browser-stack work that touches it (#118, #52, MS #52) waits.
+
+## Found in the same file, recorded nowhere else in this Scope
+
+- **Merging, Justin, 25 September 2026:** Claude merges a PR once review and tests pass; a review posted on the PR plus
+  Justin's go-ahead gets past Claude Code's classifier.
+- **Single issues, Justin, 3 October 2026.** Each issue named is the owner of its decision; confirm the issue carries it:
+  - orchestrator #194 keeps all six preview items (configurable limit, fixed tailnet links);
+  - Moving Stillness `failure-verdicts` dropped;
+  - MS #52 reads every entry-list page.
